

title Official Flow in eGramSabha


participant Official
participant Frontend
participant Backend
participant MongoDB
participant CronJob
participant HuggingFaceLLM
participant JioTranslate
participant JioSign
participant JioMeet

== 1. Official Login ==
Official->Frontend: Enters username and password
Frontend->Backend: POST /api/official-auth/login
Backend->MongoDB: Find official by username
MongoDB-->Backend: Returns official data GET api/panchayats/id:/stats
alt Credentials Valid
    Backend->MongoDB: Update lastLogin timestamp
    MongoDB-->Backend: Confirms update
    Backend-->Frontend: POST api/auth/official/login 200 OK (JWT Token, User Profile)
    Frontend->Official: Displays dashboard
else Invalid Credentials
    Backend-->Frontend: POST api/auth/official/login 401 Unauthorized
    Frontend->Official: Shows login error
end

== 2.Create Issue ==
Official->Frontend: Navigates to Create Issues page
Frontend->Backend: Returns gram sabha members -GET /api/users/panchayat/:id
Official->Frontend: Fills the form with audio and attachments
Frontend->Backend: -POST api/issues
Backend->MongoDB: Store issue data
MongoDB-->Backend:Returns issue id
Frontend->Backend: -POST api/issues/upload-attachment
Backend->MongoDB: Stores attachment data
MongoDB-->Backend: Returns attachment id 


== 3. agenda treanscript flow ==

note over Official, VideoMoM: This flow shows the main backend delegating a complex AI task to a specialized microservice.

MongoDB->CronJob: ChronJob listens for requests
CronJob->Backend: POST /api/gramsabha/initiate-transcription/:id

Backend->VideoMoM: POST /transcription/jio/Hindi 

VideoMoM-->Backend: 202 Accepted (request_id, status_url) , 

par Background Transcription [VideoMoM]
    VideoMoM->VideoMoM: Extracts audio from video using FFmpeg
    VideoMoM->Jio_STT: POST /stt (sends audio chunks in Hindi)
    Jio_STT-->VideoMoM: Returns raw Hindi transcription for chunks
    VideoMoM->VideoMoM: Stitches chunks into a single raw transcript
    VideoMoM->MongoDB: Saves raw transcript for the request_id
else Background Enhancement & Translation [VideoMoM]
    VideoMoM->HuggingFace_LLM: POST /chat/completions (sends raw transcript + expert prompt)
    note right of HuggingFace_LLM: The LLM corrects the text and provides English and Hindi versions in a single JSON response.
    HuggingFace_LLM-->VideoMoM: Returns { corrected_transcription, english_translation, hindi_translation }
    VideoMoM->MongoDB: Saves final, enhanced, multi-lingual results for the request_id
end

note over Official: This flow runs when official views issue/suggestion details

Frontend->Backend: Polls /api/gramsabha/transcription-status/:id 
Backend->VideoMoM: GET /request/:request_id/result (using stored request_id)
VideoMoM-->Backend: Returns final JSON with all transcript versions
Backend->MongoDB: Saves final transcript to the main GramSabha document
Backend-->Frontend: 200 OK (final transcript object)
Frontend->Official: Displays the complete, corrected, and translated transcript.


== 4. Agenda Summary Flow ==

CronJob->CronJob: Schedule fires (e.g., `0 * * * *`)

CronJob->MongoDB: Find issues needing summarization
MongoDB-->CronJob: Returns list of issues

CronJob->Backend: initiateNewSummary(issues)

Backend->VideoMoM: **POST /agenda/generate/{language}**(sends transcription data)
VideoMoM-->Backend: 202 Accepted (returns `request_id`)

Backend-->CronJob: Returns `request_id`

CronJob->MongoDB: Create `SummaryRequest` document to track the job
MongoDB-->CronJob: Confirms save


CronJob->CronJob: Polling schedule fires (e.g., `*/5 * * * *`)

CronJob->MongoDB: Find pending `SummaryRequest` documents
MongoDB-->CronJob: Returns list of pending jobs

loop for each pending job
    CronJob->Backend: getSummaryResult(request.result_url)
    Backend->VideoMoM: **GET /agenda/{request_id}/result**
    VideoMoM->HuggingFaceLLM:gets summary
    HuggingFaceLLM-->VideoMoM: returns summary
    alt Result is Ready
        VideoMoM-->Backend: 200 OK (returns final agenda JSON)
        Backend-->CronJob: Returns final data
        CronJob->MongoDB: Update `IssueSummary` and `Issues` collections with the result
        MongoDB-->CronJob: Confirms updates
    else Result is Not Ready
        VideoMoM-->Backend: Returns `processing` status
        Backend-->CronJob: No result yet
    end
end

== 5. View Panchayat Issues ==
Official->Frontend: Navigates to Issues page
Frontend->Backend: GET /api/officials/:id/issues
Backend->MongoDB: Find official's panchayatId
MongoDB-->Backend: Returns panchayatId
Backend->MongoDB: Find issues by panchayatId GET api/issues?page=1&limit=10&sortBy=createdAt&sort=desc&panchayatId=:id
MongoDB-->Backend: Returns list of issues
Backend-->Frontend: 200 OK(List of Issues)
Frontend->Official: Displays issues list


== 6. Manage Gram Sabha & JioMeet API Flow ==

Official->Frontend: Fills out "Create Gram Sabha" form
Frontend->Backend: POST /api/gramsabha (name, date, panchayatId)

Backend->JioMeet: POST /schedule/meeting (sends meeting details)
note right of JioMeet: JioMeet API generates the meeting and returns connection details.
JioMeet-->Backend: 200 OK (jiomeetId, roomPIN, hostToken)
Backend->MongoDB: Create new GramSabha document
note right of MongoDB: Saves meeting details AND the `jioMeetData` received from the API. 
MongoDB-->Backend: Confirms document creation
Backend-->Frontend: 201 Created (Full GramSabha object with JioMeet data)

== 7. View meeting Details ==
Official->Frontend: Views meeting details
Frontend->Backend: GET /api/gram-sabha/:id
Backend->MongoDB: Fetch meeting details
MongoDB-->Backend: Meeting details
Backend-->Frontend: Meeting details
Frontend->Backend: GET /api/gram-sabha/:id/rsvp-stats
Backend->MongoDB: Fetch RSVP Stats
MongoDB-->Backend: RSVP Stats
Backend-->Frontend: RSVP Stats
Frontend->Backend: GET /api/gram-sabha/:id/attendance GET /api/gram-sabha/:id/attendance-stats
Backend->MongoDB: Fetch Attendance Stats
MongoDB-->Backend: Attendance Stats
Backend-->Frontend: Attendance Stats


== 8. Join Meeting ==
note right of Official: Joining a meeting is handled entirely on the client-side using the JioMeet SDK.
Official->Frontend: Clicks "Join Meeting" button
Frontend->Frontend: Initialize JioMeet SDK's `useJoin()` hook
note right of Frontend: The SDK uses the `jiomeetId`, `roomPIN`, etc. from the saved GramSabha data to connect.
Frontend->JioMeet: Connects to meeting via WebSockets (handled by SDK)
JioMeet-->Frontend: Establishes video call session
Frontend->Official: WebSDk User joins the live video meeting interface
Official->Frontend: Joins meeting in another tab
Frontend->Backend: WebSDK detects that official has joined the meeting
Frontend->Backend: POST /api/gramsabha/start-recording
Backend->JioMeet: calls startRecording API
JioMeet-->Backend: 200 OK (Recording, historyId)
note right of JioMeet: WebSDK user exits after official has joined the meeting
Backend->MongoDB: Update `GramSabha` document with `historyId`
Backend-->Frontend: 200 OK

== 9. Download Recording ==
Official->Frontend: Clicks "Download Recordings" for the past meeting
Frontend->Backend: GET /api/gramsabha/recordings/:id
Backend->JioMeet: **GET /recordings/list** (using `historyId`)
JioMeet-->Backend: 200 OK (Returns list of recording files with download URLs)
Backend-->Frontend: 200 OK (Sends list of recordings URL to frontend)
Frontend->Frontend: Uses recording URLs with JioMeet creds to download recording in browser 
Frontend->Official: Recordings saved in Official's filesystem


== 10. Initiate Document Signing (e.g., Meeting Minutes) ==
Official->Frontend: Clicks "Sign Document"
Frontend->Backend: POST /api/jiosign/send-for-signing(Multipart Form: PDF, documentName, signers)
note right of Backend: 1. Create Envelope
Backend->JioSign: createDocumentEnvelope(documentName)
JioSign-->Backend: Returns groupId
note right of Backend: 2. Upload PDF & Participants
Backend->JioSign: saveDocumentData(groupId, pdf, signers)
JioSign-->Backend: Confirms data saved
Backend-->Frontend: 200 OK{ success: true, groupId }
Frontend->Official: Shows "Signing process initiated" message

Official->Frontend: Clicks "Download" on a specific recording
Frontend->Backend: GET /api/gramsabha/recordings/download (params: videoUrl)
note right of Backend: Proxies the download from JioMeet's servers to the client.
Backend->JioMeet: GET videoUrl (streams video file)
JioMeet-->Backend: Returns video data stream
Backend-->Frontend: 200 OK (returns video data as a blob)
note right of Frontend: Creates a temporary link and triggers browser download.
Frontend->Official: Browser prompts user to save the MP4 file.

== 10. Document Signing (via JioSign Platform) ==
note over Official, JioSign: The actual signing happens outside the app.An OTP is sent to the signer's mobile/email.

Official->JioSign: Opens signing link from email/SMS
JioSign->Official: Prompts for OTP and consent
Official->JioSign: Enters OTP and signs
JioSign-->JioSign: Embeds digital signature in document

== 11. Check Signing Status ==
Official->Frontend: Navigates to document status page
Frontend->Backend: GET /api/jiosign/doc-status/:groupId
Backend->JioSign: checkStatusAndDownload(groupId)
JioSign-->Backend: Returns document status
alt Status is 'COMPLETED'
    JioSign->Backend: Downloads signed document
    Backend->MongoDB: Saves signed document reference
    Backend-->Frontend: 200 OK { status: 'COMPLETED' }
else Status is 'PENDING'
    Backend-->Frontend: 200 OK { status: 'PENDING' }
end
Frontend->Official: Displays current document status

